From 0f585e7730437301be44df8342ccfab55a963eda Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alessandro Fontana <alessandro.fontana@pm.me>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 16:16:56 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ipa: simple, software_isp: keep the state across
 configurations

A still capture at full resolution reconfigures the camera in another
sensor mode and back, within the same acquisition. The soft IPA cleared
its whole state on every configure(): white balance back to unity,
autofocus restarting with a full sweep, exposure from scratch, and the
lens was closed on every stop.

- IPAConfigInfo carries the sensor info of the new mode and whether to
  keep the state; configure() returns the sensor controls to start the
  new mode with.
- The AGC remembers the last exposure per binning factor, restores it
  when coming back to a mode, and converts it otherwise (binningGain
  from the tuning file), written to the sensor before streaming.
- AWB, CCM and AF keep their state; the AF leaves the lens in place.
- The simple pipeline keeps the state within an acquisition and closes
  the lens when the camera is released rather than on every stop.

